6291ae7f192ab022e47493807525d5.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $5$ centered at $(-3,4)$, as shown above. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ that traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(2,4).$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $5$ centered at the point $(-3,4).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321939/field-1" "q-321939/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0346056c-cf8e-51bf-92f3-052a0948a6fa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321939"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79192/selection/c1b4fd3a0f15f3c7984f413f03a678f7a0fc8902ed1d9f059b1179516e0621a6" :answer/id #uuid "a6bda015-db44-5c8f-918e-363ef8e23925" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79192/selection/7ef55d19d31588b8bdc41bdad650f98b44b6cd6ab421c2407922ffb165706838" :answer/id #uuid "67666ee2-7893-5d32-9acd-bee7f015aae0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79192/selection/5104bcf836a34579f76c3a50a4cc2b3923e7469e038ca4f39051dbf0f6cdca72" :answer/id #uuid "40208fa8-350f-5d1a-bfb6-eb791